I closed the long-chunk training question this wake and started the next stage, which measures how accuracy changes with input length on a fixed model. Nothing is needed from you.

## Done: why long-chunk training lost accuracy (closed, still provisional until the checker re-derives it)
The comparison is two otherwise identical chains: one pre-trained on 256-token text chunks, one on 1,024-token chunks. The long-chunk chain's loss is in **how it compresses image pages**. It enters in the second training stage, the one that trains on page images.

| check | n | long minus short chunks (95% CI) | reading |
|---|---|---|---|
| Rebuild 256-token text from the compressed slots, after the image stage | 500 held-out documents | +.0006 nats/token, lower is better [−.0008, +.0019], sign test p .82 | not worse on text |
| Same check, after text-only stage 1 (earlier wake) | 500 documents | −.0018 nats/token | not worse on text |
| Rebuild a page image's words from its slots (earlier wake) | 500 pages | −8.0 pt of words [−10.6, −5.5] | worse on images |
| Text QA, ten short passages (judge accuracy) | 1,500 questions per seed | +2.3 pt (seed 42), −0.6 pt (seed 43) | no loss |
| Text QA, the same passages joined into one ~1.3k-token chunk (recorded) | 1,500 questions per seed | −1.1 pt, −3.3 pt | small loss |

- The gap between the two text layouts is +3.4 / +2.7 pt (sign test p .017 / .028). That fits "the text loss shows only on long chunks". It misses the 3-point bar at seed 43, so it is not decided.
- **Training change this points to (your call):** keep the 256-token first stage. If long chunks are tried again, change the image stage, and check page transcription before any finetune.
- One job was flagged FAILED, but it was harmless. Its first attempt finished and wrote the full result. After a requeue, the second attempt refused to overwrite that file. I added this case to the campaign's known-issues list.

## Running now: does accuracy drop as inputs get longer?
This stage uses the seed-42 reference model on the 1,500 document questions.

| cell | state |
|---|---|
| 10 pages, compressed | running |
| 20 pages, uncompressed, 300-question test (checks that the ~19.5k-token prompt fits on one GPU) | running; past model loading and generating |
| 20 pages, uncompressed, all 1,500 questions | waits for the test to pass |
| 20 pages, compressed, all 1,500 questions | waits for the test to pass |

The 4-page compressed and uncompressed results, plus the 10-page uncompressed result, already exist and will be reused.

## Next
- The next wake starts when the 20-page test and the 10-page cell finish (at most 3 hours).
- It will check their health and compute the length effect at 10 pages: the compressed-vs-uncompressed gap at 10 pages minus the same gap at 4 pages.
- It will then launch the seed-43 repeats and the text-length cells.
- Budget so far: 31 of 70 cells and about 14 of 60 GPU-hours, with about 5 more for the cells now running.

